# 🛡️ Day 33 – Media Integrity Analyzer

> Learn to evaluate information before believing it.

## 📌 Overview

The **Media Integrity Analyzer** is an interactive web application designed to improve media literacy through hands-on learning. Instead of simply teaching theory, the application allows users to analyze fictional news headlines and social media content, identify misleading language, detect emotional manipulation, and build practical critical-thinking skills.

The project is fully offline and built as a **single HTML file** using only HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

---

## 🚀 Features

### 📰 Headline Detective
- Analyze fictional news headlines
- Identify exaggerated or misleading claims
- View Headline Accuracy Score
- Compare original and rewritten headlines
- Learn why certain headlines are misleading

### 🎭 Emotion Detector
- Analyze fictional social media posts
- Detect emotional manipulation techniques
- Highlight emotionally charged words
- Discover the intended audience
- View neutral rewrites

### 📊 Live Media Integrity Metrics
- Headline Accuracy
- Source Reliability
- Emotional Manipulation
- Audience Targeting

### 📈 Media Integrity Dashboard
- Overall Media Integrity Score
- Biggest Red Flag
- Key Learning Summary
- Three practical media literacy habits
- Replay with new randomized scenarios

### 🎨 Modern UI
- Premium editorial dark theme
- Multiple color themes (including Claude Orange)
- Responsive layout
- Smooth animations
- Interactive progress indicators

